CL 1.1
P destinations-verify(): taste.observe("r12-destinations")
C taste.journey.verify r12-actual-alternate-regression: taste.observe("r12-destinations").realRegressionBound == true -- block preserve actual two-destination keyboard refusal on the unchanged Luna draft
C taste.journey.verify r12-all-destinations: taste.observe("r12-destinations").allDestinationsDelivered == true -- block all three final rare UIs actually file Check again and Discard sample as well as the main Keep proof journey
P labels-verify(): taste.observe("r12-label-export")
C taste.labels.verify r12-all-episodes-exported: taste.observe("r12-label-export").allUsedLabelsExported == true and taste.observe("r12-label-export").countsBound == true -- block every used Paul label and historical or workflow retention decision reaches the append-only export
C taste.labels.verify r12-episode-schema: taste.observe("r12-label-export").oneEpisodePerLine == true and taste.observe("r12-label-export").missingImagesExplicit == true -- block unique JSON lines preserve layer source time and explicit missing historical images
-- C13i: all Paul labels, head-free examples, frozen real-page calibration.
P probe-verify(): taste.observe("r12-probe")
C taste.probe.verify r12-real-lens-probe: taste.observe("r12-probe").boundedScope == true and taste.observe("r12-probe").realSeedBound == true and taste.observe("r12-probe").rawBound == true and taste.observe("r12-probe").twoActualEffects == true and taste.observe("r12-probe").actualViewBox == true -- block actual Sol seed lens has distinct pointer touch effects after real viewBox conversion
P filing-probe-verify(): taste.observe("r12-filing-probe")
C taste.probe.verify r12-real-file-drop: taste.observe("r12-filing-probe").identicalRealSource == true and taste.observe("r12-filing-probe").beforeActuallyUnfiled == true and taste.observe("r12-filing-probe").afterActuallyFiled == true and taste.observe("r12-filing-probe").boundedProbe == true -- block preserve real failing drops and prove actual pointer touch destination without changing the page
C taste.driver.verify r12-filed-all-modes: taste.observe("r12-driver").actualFiledJourneys == true -- block both rare UI pages actually file Keep proof in pointer keyboard touch across all four variants
P driver-verify(): taste.observe("r12-driver")
C taste.driver.verify r12-measured-stroke-coordinates: taste.observe("r12-driver").strokeTransformsMeasured == true -- block each actual SVG stroke point binds its current measured screen transform rather than a stale viewport
C taste.driver.verify r12-real-state-preparation: taste.observe("r12-driver").actualStatePreparation == true and taste.observe("r12-driver").matchedStateRecipes == true -- block both rare UI arms deliver bounded real keyboard prerequisites with observed state change; activation effect remains separate
C taste.driver.verify r12-real-targets: taste.observe("r12-driver").realTargetFailurePreserved == true and taste.observe("r12-driver").bareTargetsResolve == true -- block delivered effects resolve actual R10 bare SVG target IDs
C taste.driver.verify r12-real-svg-paths: taste.observe("r12-driver").legacyPathsDelivered == true -- block bounded actual viewBox conversion drives real pointer touch paths
C taste.driver.verify r12-driver-revision: taste.observe("r12-driver").currentDriverBindings == true -- block all final observations bind this driver revision
C taste.driver.verify r12-no-coverage-waiver: taste.observe("r12-driver").oldCoverageStillBlocks == true -- block incomplete recorded input modes remain failures
P negative-verify(): taste.observe("r12-negative")
C taste.journey.verify r12-current-routine-facts: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").routineFactsAreCurrent == true -- block stale check inputs cannot be reused and unsupported no-defect crops escalate
C taste.journey.verify r12-paid-replay-binding: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").paidRepairReplayBound == true -- block actual wrong-source replay is refused before inference; any performed replay binds original response model and usage hashes
P journey-verify(): taste.observe("r12-pipeline")
P packet-verify(): taste.observe("r12-packet")
C taste.negative.verify r12-real-regression: taste.observe("r12-negative").realCaseBindings == true and taste.observe("r12-negative").actualInference == true and taste.observe("r12-negative").regressionEscalates == true -- block a recorded real regression cannot silently pass
C taste.negative.verify r12-missing-observations: taste.observe("r12-negative").unsupportedAbstains == true -- block unsupported real page pairs abstain rather than fabricate confidence
C taste.journey.verify r12-six-completed-pages: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").sixCompletedPages == true -- block both matched pages complete in Sol Luna and fusion arms
C taste.journey.verify r12-source-render-bindings: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").sourceRenderCheckBindings == true -- block actual source and four screenshot hashes bind the final checks
C taste.journey.verify r12-real-controls: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").actualControlJourneys == true -- block actual light dark desktop and phone controls pass with complete coverage
C taste.journey.verify r12-blocking-checks: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").blockingChecksPassed == true -- block spelling overflow centring and geometry pass measured page checks
C taste.journey.verify r12-initial-newlines: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").initialNewlineConversionBound == true -- block four legacy first inputs bind exact LF to CRLF conversion; actual wrong-task source is refused
C taste.journey.verify r12-accepted-source: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").sameStartingSources == true -- block identical seed content with only the declared initial newline conversion; all later accepted bytes and reversions remain exact
C taste.journey.verify r12-every-round-gated: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").everyFusionRoundGated == true -- block live CPU inference gates every Luna repair and records every routine decision
C taste.journey.verify r12-crop-used: taste.observe("r12-pipeline").selectedCropsReachCritic == true -- block selected localized images and all four theme viewport images reach the real final critic
C taste.packet.verify r12-blind-packet: taste.observe("r12-packet").twentyFourBlindShots == true and taste.observe("r12-packet").bothThemesAndArms == true -- block all three pairwise blind A B comparisons in dark and light bind actual screenshot bytes
C taste.packet.verify r12-accounting: taste.observe("r12-packet").measuredUsage == true and taste.observe("r12-packet").noInventedCallSavings == true and taste.observe("r12-packet").calibrationCostsIncluded == true -- block actual metered calls include calibration and only observed omitted critic calls
C taste.packet.verify r12-model-ablation: taste.observe("r12-packet").baseModelBoundaryVisible == true -- block episode retrieval and frozen model contributions remain distinct
P personal-verify(): taste.observe("r12-personal"); taste.observe("r12-real")
C taste.personal.verify r12-all-votes: taste.observe("r12-personal").votesComplete == true -- block every exported identity and quality vote participates
C taste.personal.verify r12-all-reasons: taste.observe("r12-personal").reasonsComplete == true -- block every feedback reason is a separately labelled aspect example
C taste.personal.verify r12-earlier-rounds: taste.observe("r12-personal").earlierRoundsPresent == true and taste.observe("r12-personal").identityLabels >= 25 -- block recover all earlier recorded votes and answer keys read-only
C taste.personal.verify r12-aspects: taste.observe("r12-personal").allSevenAspects == true -- block motion voice overflow centring spelling geometry polish
C taste.personal.verify r12-provenance: taste.observe("r12-personal").sourceHashesMatch == true -- block retained labels bind original source bytes
C taste.personal.verify r12-no-personal-head: taste.observe("r12-personal").headFree == true and taste.observe("r12-personal").identitiesRemainDistinct == true -- block sparse identity labels cannot become quality training
C taste.personal.verify r12-retrieved-reasons: taste.observe("r12-personal").retrievesReasons == true and taste.observe("r12-personal").textEmbeddingNormalized == true -- block normalized embedding retrieval returns reason texts
C taste.personal.verify r12-real-pages: taste.observe("r12-real").realObscura == true and taste.observe("r12-real").allDecisionKinds == true -- block gate cases come from actual page runs
C taste.personal.verify r12-isolation: taste.observe("r12-real").heldoutIsR11 == true and taste.observe("r12-real").groupsDisjoint == true and taste.observe("r12-real").pixelsDisjoint == true -- block independent page groups and exact pixels stay outside calibration
C taste.personal.verify r12-no-label-leak: taste.observe("r12-real").noAfterScoreInInputs == true and taste.observe("r12-real").realRepairHeldout >= 20 -- block held-out critic outcomes are labels only
P gate-verify(): taste.observe("r12-gate")
P calibration-verify(): taste.observe("r12-calibration")
P font-verify(): taste.observe("r12-fonts")
C taste.font.verify r12-real-font-false-positives: taste.observe("r12-fonts").actualFontLabelsAccepted == true and taste.observe("r12-fonts").realFalsePositivesCaptured == true -- block real font names and valid unfiled status remain readable
C taste.font.verify r12-font-typos-blocked: taste.observe("r12-fonts").nearMissesBlocked == true and taste.observe("r12-fonts").noCitationWaiver == true -- block exact font-name admission cannot waive misspellings
C taste.calibration.verify r12-calibration-bound: taste.observe("r12-calibration").frozenRowsMatch == true and taste.observe("r12-calibration").allGatesQualified == true -- block calibrate routine decisions before held-out admission
C taste.calibration.verify r12-failed-routes-visible: taste.observe("r12-calibration").firstAttemptDeactivated == true and taste.observe("r12-calibration").subjectiveNotQualified == true and taste.observe("r12-calibration").noHeadTraining == true -- block preserve failed subjective-quality routes and keep personal conditioning head-free
C taste.gate.verify r12-gate-bindings: taste.observe("r12-gate").calibrationBound == true and taste.observe("r12-gate").heldoutBound == true -- block calibration is frozen before independent held-out admission
C taste.gate.verify r12-live-inference: taste.observe("r12-gate").frozenModelIdentity == true and taste.observe("r12-gate").actualInference == true -- block real CPU LAYA answers every recorded request
C taste.gate.verify r12-repair-qualified: taste.observe("r12-gate").repairAdmitted == true and taste.observe("r12-gate").repairCoverage >= 0.5 and taste.observe("r12-gate").repairAccuracy >= 0.9 -- block answer most comparable-check retention decisions; subjective critic agreement remains separate
C taste.gate.verify r12-failure-qualified: taste.observe("r12-gate").failureAdmitted == true -- block independently validate real check triage
C taste.gate.verify r12-crop-qualified: taste.observe("r12-gate").cropAdmitted == true -- block independently validate critic crop selection
-- C13h: Sol concept/draft/final crops; Luna reading/implementation/repairs; live LAYA every render.
P fusion(brief, files): taste.research(brief); taste.concept(brief); taste.page.write(files); taste.render(files); taste.gate(files); taste.repair(files, against="previous"); taste.finish(files)
A taste.observe(case:str) -> facts -- host-owned CL observations in taste_contracts.py, no new test files
P fusion-verify(): taste.observe("r11")
C taste.fusion.verify r11-live-laya: taste.observe("r11").liveLaya == true -- block C13h: the owned service actually answers on assigned port 48809
C taste.fusion.verify r11-verify: taste.observe("r11").verifyRan == true -- block C13h: triage is checked by efficiency.laya_verify's native implementation
C taste.fusion.verify r11-bilingual: taste.observe("r11").bilingualCorrect == true -- block C13h: correct English and French survive offline dictionaries
C taste.fusion.verify r11-typos: taste.observe("r11").typosBlocked == true -- block C13h: actual misspellings block completion
C taste.fusion.verify r11-layer-separation: taste.observe("r11").separateLayers == true -- block C13h: personal votes never enter corrective learning
C taste.fusion.verify r11-personal-abstention: taste.observe("r11").personalAbstains == true -- block C13h: sparse personal labels cannot authorize a confident answer
C taste.fusion.verify r11-jevbench: taste.observe("r11").jevbenchFloor == true -- block C13h: complete public corpus remains at least 138 of 231
C taste.fusion.verify r11-public-learning: taste.observe("r11").publicCases >= 9 -- block C13h: public licensed evidence participates in corrective learning
C taste.fusion.verify r11-history-learning: taste.observe("r11").historicalCases >= 1 -- block C13h: real r6-r10 repairs participate in corrective learning
C taste.fusion.verify r11-box-negative: taste.observe("corrective-render").badBox == true -- block C13h: Obscura detects text outside its real button
C taste.fusion.verify r11-box-positive: taste.observe("corrective-render").goodBox == true -- block C13h: a fitted label passes
C taste.fusion.verify r11-center-negative: taste.observe("corrective-render").badCenter == true -- block C13h: off-center figure fails
C taste.fusion.verify r11-center-positive: taste.observe("corrective-render").goodCenter == true -- block C13h: centered figure passes
C taste.fusion.verify r11-render-spelling: taste.observe("corrective-render").badSpelling == true and taste.observe("corrective-render").goodSpelling == true -- block C13h: actual rendered typo fails and corrected bilingual copy passes
C taste.fusion.verify r11-node-label: taste.observe("corrective-render").badNodeLabel == true -- block C13h: a semantic node label must fit its measured node
C taste.fusion.verify r11-decorative-overlap: taste.observe("corrective-render").decorativeOverlapAccepted == true -- block C13h: illustrative overlays are not inferred to be diagram nodes
C taste.fusion.verify r11-four-arms: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").fourArms == true -- block C13h: both tasks have real sealed evidence for both arms
C taste.fusion.verify r11-cost-caps: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").budgets == true -- block C13h: every recorded provider call remains in the declared task dollar ceiling
C taste.fusion.verify r11-blind-binding: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").blindBound == true -- block C13h: all eight A/B screenshots match the selected artifact receipts
C taste.fusion.verify r11-archive-binding: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").archivesBound == true -- block C13h: every archived raw entry matches its digest; runtime profiles and seal keys are absent; bundles stay below 100 MB
C taste.fusion.verify r11-split-isolation: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").splitsDisjoint == true -- block C13h: underlying screens cannot cross train, calibration and held-out splits
C taste.fusion.verify r11-visible-labels: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").distinctPixels == true -- block C13h: identical captured pixels remain runtime evidence and cannot train a visual preference
C taste.fusion.verify r11-pixel-variants: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").fourPixelVariants == true -- block C13h: actual dark/light desktop/phone crops compare with the bound reference and previous round
C taste.fusion.verify r11-regression-veto: taste.observe("r11-regression").vetoed == true and taste.observe("r11-regression").headRetained == true -- block C13h: a wrong-label fit on real frozen pixels is vetoed and leaves the admitted head unchanged
C taste.fusion.verify r11-after-floor: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").afterFloor == true -- block C13h: the post-change complete JevBench corpus retains 138 of 231 or better
C taste.fusion.verify r11-learning-regression: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").regressionProtected == true -- block C13h: reject a weaker candidate and retain the previous admitted head
C taste.fusion.verify r11-calibrated-only: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").calibratedOnly == true -- block C13h: pixel answers require the calibrated confidence lower bound, otherwise abstain
C taste.fusion.verify r11-calibrated-answer: taste.observe("r11-vision-gate").qualifiedHeldoutCases > 0 and taste.observe("r11-vision-gate").bidirectional == true -- block C13h: real held-out pixels yield the correct forward and reverse answer above the gate
C taste.fusion.verify r11-calibrated-abstention: taste.observe("r11-vision-gate").sameAbstains == true and taste.observe("r11-vision-gate").websiteAbstains == true -- block C13h: identical pixels and unsupported website dimensions abstain
C taste.fusion.verify r11-online-splits: taste.observe("r11-learning-policy").newLabelsReachAllSplits == true and taste.observe("r11-learning-policy").groupStable == true and taste.observe("r11-learning-policy").heldoutFrozen == true -- block C13h: new personal labels can calibrate a head; repeat groups stay together; admitted held-out membership stays frozen
C taste.fusion.verify r11-live-audit: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").liveAudited == true -- block C13h: LAYA actually ran; retrospective repairs remain explicitly marked
C taste.fusion.verify r11-measured-savings: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").noInventedSavings == true -- block C13h: no skipped call means zero proven time saved
C taste.fusion.verify r11-completion-truth: taste.observe("r11-pipeline").honestCompletion == true -- block C13h: blocking artifacts cannot be labelled complete
X Introduce spelling, box fit and centering in that order, one new requirement per accepted round; all three required at finish.
X Revert repairs that lower measured quality; preserve their spend and rejected renders. Newly failing checks still block finish and enter subsequent repairs.
X Pixel scores and public synthetic perturbation accuracy are bounded diagnostics, never proof of general taste or 2D-to-3D skill.
-- taste: executable manual for taste that holds (plan 20 C13.6 and C13.7). Written by Claude as Neyvia's design lead, 4 Oct 2026.
-- Why it exists: in round 3 Paul told the arms apart at once. Luna's landing was a clean generic template (empty columns,
-- a watermark letter, stock slogans); Luna's "rare UI" page used six common patterns (command palette, split view, slider,
-- hold button, tree, radial menu) in mostly empty panels and failed the brief. Claude's page took one subject (fungi), used
-- thirteen elements from HCI papers (magic lens, bubble cursor, marking menu, alphaslider, crossing, pull cord) and drew a
-- plate for each. The gap was research, concept, content and finish, not CSS.
-- Core idea (Paul, 22:35): taste is not a plugin. Draft once, then question the draft against a better result, write the
-- difference down as a record, turn it into lessons, and make targeted repairs. First drafts are slow; repairs are fast.
-- Runs with: manuals/skills/no-slop.cl (words), manuals/skills/deliverables.cl (finish), manuals/skills/design-craft.cl (Neyvia
-- components only). Host harness (Codex, C13.1-4): scripts/c13_render.mjs (render and drive), src/grant_agent/taste_judge.py
-- (frozen pairwise judge, lesson admission). Every C below names the observer that decides it; the critique rubric is the last section.
-- Studied, not copied: anthropics/claude-code plugins/frontend-design (SKILL.md v1.1.0, "All rights reserved", commercial terms):
-- ideas only, no text. Ideas taken: subject vernacular as the source of a distinct look, a design plan reviewed against the
-- default before code, a named list of generated-page clusters, one bold element, one orchestrated motion, numbering only for
-- real sequences, screenshot self-critique, remove one accessory before shipping.

-- L0
L taste v1 tools:taste.render,taste.critique,taste.diff -- research the uncommon, one concept, specific content, no empty panels, then difference-and-repair rounds until the critique and the anchor pass

-- L1 model view (the host renders it from the contract below: procedures first, their goals, the choices, the actions, 3 pitfalls).
-- Shown here as comments for review; the cl_skill runner reads the contract lines, and each G is written there as C <procedure> goal.
--   P taste.make(brief, files) G: taste.gate(files).blocks == 0 and taste.critique(files).passed and taste.anchor(files).verdict in ["tie", "win"] and taste.rounds() >= 2
--   P taste.repair(files, against) G: taste.diff.rows_open() == 0 and taste.critique(files).mean >= previous.mean and taste.churn(files).ratio <= 0.5
--   P taste.research(brief) G: len(taste.research.used()) >= taste.brief(brief).count and taste.research.primary_share() >= 0.5 and len(taste.research.candidates()) >= 2 * len(taste.research.used())
--   P taste.concept(brief) G: taste.concept.ready() and taste.concept.before_layout()
--   P taste.finish(files) G: taste.gate(files).blocks == 0 and taste.render(files).dead == 0 and taste.render(files).errors == 0 and taste.critique(files).passed
--   J against "anchor"|"other-arm"|"paul"|"previous": "Which better result is this round measured against?"
--   J cause "research"|"concept"|"content"|"density"|"visual"|"motion"|"type"|"color"|"spacing"|"finish"|"broken": "Where does this gap come from?"
--   J scope "element"|"section"|"page": "How much must change to close this gap?"
--   J lesson "promote"|"local"|"drop": "Would this gap repeat on the next brief of this kind?"
--   A taste.render(files, viewports?: "desktop"|"phone"|"both", themes?: "light"|"dark"|"both") -> render[variant dead errors overflow emptyPanels blankRegions shots]
--   A taste.critique(files, against?) -> critique[axis score evidence fix]
--   A taste.diff.write(files, against) -> diff[axis gap ours better evidence cause repair scope] ~
--   A taste.lesson(row, rule, check) -> lesson ~
--   A taste.gate(files) -> gate[check level hits]
--   A taste.anchor(files) -> verdict[anchor verdict reason]
--   X a first render is a draft, never done; look at the screenshots before you claim anything
--   X repair the rows of the difference report; a rewrite throws away the parts that already work
--   X a common pattern with a new name is still common; rare means a primary source and its defining mechanism working

-- states (the host keeps these as CL records in the task workspace; the agent writes the ones marked ~)
-- taste-research.cl ~
S taste.research h1 #n [name kind source sourceKind year common used why]
-- taste-concept.cl ~ (written before the first page file; the host checks the order)
S taste.concept h2 #1 [idea subject vernacular bold quiet motion rejected]
-- render/<round>/report.json (host, scripts/c13_render.mjs)
S taste.render h3 #4 [variant dead errors overflow emptyPanels blankRegions families bodyMeasure bodySize hues contrastFails trackedCaps autoMotion reducedMotionRunning shots]
-- critique/<round>.cl (critic model, image input)
S taste.critique h4 #11 [axis score evidence fix]
-- taste-diff-<round>.cl ~ (the difference report: the core record, format below)
S taste.diff h5 #n [axis gap ours better evidence cause repair scope]
-- lessons: M lines appended to the diff file, state quarantine, admitted only through the C9 no-regression gate
S taste.rounds h6 #n [round kind seconds critiqueMean gateBlocks anchorVerdict churn]

-- difference report format (CL record; one file per round: taste-diff-<round>.cl)
-- header: S taste.diff #<rows> against=<anchor|other-arm|paul|previous>:"<path or quote>" round=<n> ours="<path>"
-- one E row per gap, positional by [axis gap ours better evidence cause repair scope]:
--   axis     one rubric axis name (fidelity concept content density illustration motion type color spacing finish)
--   gap      0..4: how far ours is behind on this axis (4 = the better result does what ours fails to do at all)
--   ours     what ours does, observed, in one line ("6 specimens, each a stock widget with a 1-line demo")
--   better   what the better result does on the same axis, observed ("13 plates from HCI papers, one subject")
--   evidence two refs the critic can check: a screenshot tile and a selector or line, one for each side
--   cause    one of the J cause values
--   repair   one targeted edit, imperative, naming the element ("replace .wheel demo with a marking menu: expert mark without menu")
--   scope    element|section|page; page is allowed once per task and only for cause concept or research
-- keep rows: gap 0, cause "keep", repair "leave": what ours already does as well or better; the repair does not touch them
-- then M lesson lines: M taste "<rule in one sentence>" src:taste-diff-<round>.cl#<row> check:"<the C or J that would catch it>" author:<agent> state:quarantine
-- example (round 1 of the manual-only proof, Luna's round-3 page against Claude's):
--   S taste.diff #3 against=other-arm:"proof/r6-blind/arm-c/rare-ui.html" round=1 ours="rare-ui.html"
--   E "fidelity" 4 "6 patterns, all in widget libraries (cmdk, kbar, Radix)" "13 elements, each cited to a paper or HCI archive" "ours d-light.t0 #specimen-02; better d-light.t0 .plate-sources" "research" "replace launcher, split view and tree with 3 elements from the candidates table" "section"
--   E "density" 3 "radial panel shows one 'open' disc in 360 px of blank" "every plate shows its subject at rest" "ours d-light.t0 #wheel; better d-light.t1 #bubble" "density" "draw the wheel's 6 actions at rest, faded, around the disc" "element"
--   E "color" 0 "warm paper palette and serif headings read as a field notebook" "same family of choices" "ours d-light.t0 body; better d-light.t0 body" "keep" "leave" "page"
--   M taste "a demo panel shows its content at rest, before any input" src:taste-diff-1.cl#2 check:"C taste.make rest-content" author:luna state:quarantine

-- host (archival contract; the model view above is what the agent sees)
T variant{viewport:desktop|phone theme:light|dark}
T render{variant:variant dead:int errors:int overflow:int emptyPanels:[str] blankRegions:[str] families:[str] bodyMeasure:int bodySize:num bodyLeading:num hues:int contrastFails:int trackedCaps:int autoMotion:int reducedMotionRunning:int leftEdges:int sectionPads:int heroVisual:num shots:[path]}
T panel{selector:str area:int ink:num gap:num atRest:bool}
T source{url:str kind:paper|archive|author-repo|demo|article|pattern-library|docs resolves:bool|null}
T candidate{name:str kind:str sources:[source] year:int|null common:bool used:bool why:str}
T concept{idea:str subject:str vernacular:[str] bold:str quiet:[str] motion:str|null rejected:[str] writtenAt:time}
T critique{axis:str score:0..4 evidence:[str] fix:str}
T diffrow{axis:str gap:0..4 ours:str better:str evidence:[str] cause:str repair:str scope:element|section|page}
T lesson{rule:str src:str check:str author:str state:quarantine|verified|reverted}
T round{round:int kind:draft|repair|finish seconds:int critiqueMean:num gateBlocks:int anchorVerdict:lose|tie|win|null churn:num}

A taste.brief(brief:str) -> {adjectives:[str] count:int|null subjectGiven:bool deliverable:str} -- the brief's key words become checks: rare, beautiful, working, credited, simple, fast; count = the number the brief states; a vague quantity ("a lot", "many") is answered in the concept with a number the page can build to its mechanism (a task policy may set a floor); a brief with no quantity (a landing page) has count null, and no other brief's count carries over
I taste.brief reads:task
A taste.render(files:[path] viewports?:[desktop phone] themes?:[light dark]) -> [render] -- Neyvia's own browser only: the non-stealth Obscura engine (browser_obscura.py) on the agent side, explicit port 48801-48809, never a visible window and never a substitute browser; gaps that block a measure are reported, not filled by another engine (proof/c13-browser-gaps.md); walks the page like a reader (scroll in 60% steps, settle 2.5 s) before measuring, so reveals and lazy canvases run; captures in viewport steps, never one full-page resize (a resize blanked Claude's speed-zoom canvas in round 3)
I taste.render reads:files cost:"5-15 s per page and width on Obscura" impl:scripts/c13_render.mjs prototype:proof/c13-taste/tools/oshot.py
A taste.drive(files:[path]) -> {controls:int exercised:int dead:[str] focusInvisible:[str] keyboardOnly:[str]} -- every interactive element by pointer, keyboard and touch through CDP Input events on Obscura; dead = no DOM, style, scroll or pixel change within 600 ms; an engine gap (a missing API such as setPointerCapture) is reported as undecided, never as dead
I taste.drive reads:files impl:scripts/c13_render.mjs
A taste.panels(files:[path]) -> [panel] -- innermost section, article, figure, [role=region] or demo container taller than 120 px: ink = share of an 8 px grid covered by text boxes, media, controls and drawn pixels; gap = tallest empty horizontal band / panel height; measured at rest after the reader walk (prototype: proof/c13-taste/tools/measure.cjs)
I taste.panels reads:files
A taste.text(files:[path]) -> {words:int concrete:int stock:[str] numbering:[str] eyebrows:int} -- visible text only; concrete = numbers with units, proper nouns not at sentence start, code, dates, named sources
I taste.text reads:files
A taste.sources(files:[path]) -> [source] -- every outbound link and citation; kind by domain and form (doi.org, dl.acm.org, ieeexplore, arxiv, *.edu, lab pages and HCI archives = paper|archive; the original author's repo = author-repo; WAI-ARIA APG, MDN, Radix, shadcn, Material, HIG = pattern-library); resolves checked when the host has network, else null
I taste.sources reads:files net:"HEAD only, when allowed"
A taste.common(names:[str]) -> [{name:str common:bool listedAs:str}] -- against config/c13/commonness.json (seed list in F below); also common when the only sources are pattern libraries
I taste.common reads:config
A taste.research.write(rows:[candidate]) -> path ~ -- writes taste-research.cl
I taste.research.write writes:workspace undo:"keep the previous file"
A taste.concept.write(concept:concept) -> path ~ -- writes taste-concept.cl; the host stamps writtenAt
I taste.concept.write writes:workspace undo:"keep the previous file"
A taste.concept.ready() -> bool -- the record has all fields, idea <= 25 words, >= 3 vernacular words that the page copy uses (a padded list of terms the page never shows is a proxy, not a concept), >= 1 rejected default
A taste.concept.before_layout() -> bool -- writtenAt is earlier than the first write of any deliverable page file
A taste.coverage(files:[path]) -> num -- share of sections whose visible text contains at least one vernacular word from the concept
I taste.coverage reads:files,workspace
A taste.critique(files:[path] against?:path) -> [critique] -- the critic model gets the brief, the concept record, the desktop light first screen, full-page tiles (1800 px) for desktop light, phone light and desktop dark, the drive report, and the anchor's tiles; it scores the rubric below and must cite a tile and region per score
I taste.critique reads:files,workspace,anchors cost:"1 image-input call, about 12 images"
A taste.anchor(files:[path]) -> {anchor:path verdict:lose|tie|win reason:str} -- frozen pairwise judge (C9.3, taste_judge.py) plus the critic's side-by-side of the two screenshot sets; the anchor is picked from proof/taste-anchors by brief kind
I taste.anchor reads:files,anchors impl:src/grant_agent/taste_judge.py
A taste.diff.write(files:[path] against:path|str) -> path ~ -- the difference report record above; against is a file, an anchor id, Paul's words, or the previous round's file
I taste.diff.write writes:workspace undo:"the report is append-only per round"
A taste.diff.rows_open() -> int -- rows with gap >= 2 whose repair has not been applied and re-checked
A taste.lesson(row:str rule:str check:str) -> lesson ~ -- quarantined; the C9 Evolver re-runs the source task and the frozen suite before it can be promoted into this manual
A taste.labels() -> {identityKnown:int qualityDecisive:int qualityTies:int qualityUnknown:int qualityRuns:int} -- blind-vote labels by kind: identityGuess (which side Paul called Claude) and qualityPreference (C, L, tie or unknown); an unknown stays unknown
I taste.labels reads:proof/preference-pairs.json impl:src/grant_agent/taste_labels.py
A taste.judge() -> {labelKind:str agreement:num|null majorityBaseline:num|null total:int} -- the frozen quality judge's leave-one-out calibration (config/c13-judge.json); the identity judge (config/c13-identity-judge.json) measures recognizability and never promotes
I taste.judge reads:config impl:src/grant_agent/taste_judge.py
I taste.lesson writes:manual-frontier deps:[src/grant_agent/taste_judge.py:admit_lesson] undo:"one-click revert by lineage"
A taste.churn(files:[path]) -> {ratio:num rowsTouched:int unmapped:int} -- changed lines / previous lines since the last round; unmapped = changed hunks no diff row asks for
I taste.churn reads:files,history
A taste.overlap(files:[path] against:path) -> {numbers:num elements:num phrases:num} -- share of ours that also appears in against: distinctive numbers, element names from the research table, 6-word phrases
I taste.overlap reads:files
A taste.rounds() -> int -- completed critique-and-fix rounds this task
A taste.gate(files:[path]) -> [{check:str level:block|warn|note hits:[str]}] -- every C below plus no-slop and deliverables
A taste.page.write(files:[path]) -> [path] ~ -- write or repair the page; every C below runs on the result
I taste.page.write writes:files deps:[manuals/skills/no-slop.cl manuals/skills/deliverables.cl] undo:"keep the previous round's file until the new round passes"

-- research depth: find the uncommon, read primary sources
C taste.research.write candidates: len([c for c in taste.research.candidates()]) >= 2 * len(taste.research.used()) -- block plan20#C13.3: look at twice as many candidates as you use; the first idea is usually the common one; research runs only when the brief asks for it (rare, sourced, credited), never for a landing page
C taste.research.write rare-only: len([u for u in taste.research.used() if taste.common([u.name])[0].common]) == 0 -- block plan20#C13.3+paul/r6: when the brief says rare, nothing from the commonness list ships (command palette, split view, slider, hold button, tree, radial menu were the round-3 failure)
C taste.page.write primary-sources: taste.research.primary_share() >= 0.5 -- block plan20#C13.3: at least half the used elements cite a paper, an HCI archive or the inventor's own repo, not a blog or a pattern library
C taste.page.write credited-in-place: len([u for u in taste.research.used() if not u.creditedInSection]) == 0 -- block r6/tasks#T2: each element's credit sits in its own section, with author, venue and year when there is one
C taste.page.write mechanism: taste.critique(files).axis("fidelity").score >= 3 -- block plan20#C13.3: each rare element shows its defining mechanism (a marking menu works by mark without the menu; a bubble cursor always captures the nearest target)
C taste.page.write sources-resolve: len([s for s in taste.sources(files) if s.resolves == false]) == 0 -- warn: every cited link loads; null (no network) is reported, not failed

-- concept before layout: one strong idea
C taste.concept.write ready: taste.concept.ready() -- block plan20#C13.6: one idea in <= 25 words, the subject, 3+ words of its vernacular that the page will use, the one bold element, what stays quiet, the defaults rejected
C taste.page.write concept-first: taste.concept.before_layout() -- block plan20#C13.6: the concept record exists before the first page file
C taste.page.write concept-coverage: taste.coverage(files) >= 0.6 -- block r6/claude-vs-luna: the subject runs through at least 60% of sections; six unrelated specimens is a list, not a concept
C taste.page.write concept-legible: taste.critique(files).axis("concept").score >= 3 -- block: the critic names the idea from the first screen alone and it matches the record
C taste.page.write one-bold: taste.critique(files).axis("concept").evidence_count("competing bold") == 0 -- warn frontend-design(idea): boldness in one place; everything around it disciplined

-- specific content instead of stock phrases
C taste.page.write stock: len(taste.text(files).stock) == 0 -- block paul/r6+no-slop: no slogan that fits any page (list in F; "Think with care", "Make things real", "what comes next", "curated for the curious", "in motion", "at the center")
C taste.page.write concrete: taste.text(files).concrete * 100 >= 4 * taste.text(files).words -- warn: at least 4 concrete tokens per 100 words, section numbering excluded (a 4,000-line module, 1993, Xerox PARC); a regex count did not separate the round-3 landings (2.2 each), so the critic's swap test is the block
C taste.page.write swap-test: taste.critique(files).axis("content").evidence_count("swappable") <= 1 -- block: the critic finds at most one heading or line that would fit an unrelated page unchanged
C taste.page.write real-sequence: len(taste.text(files).numbering) == 0 or taste.critique(files).axis("content").evidence_count("fake sequence") == 0 -- warn frontend-design(idea): 01/02/03 markers only when the content is a sequence
C taste.page.write no-invented: len(text.match(pattern:"(?i)\\b(trusted by|\\d+k\\+ (users|teams)|99\\.9+%|as seen (on|in))\\b" in:all)) == 0 -- block antislop#R-17: no invented proof

-- density: no empty panels
C taste.page.write empty-panel: len([p for p in taste.panels(files) if p.ink < 0.20 or p.gap > 0.33]) == 0 -- block plan20#C13.2+r6/luna-rare-ui: no panel is mostly blank; measured on round 3 (box measure; Edge prototype, Obscura agrees for Luna): Luna's wheel panel ink 0.06, its launcher, split and hold panels have empty bands of 0.31 to 0.38; Claude's plates 0.02 to 0.26 except one
C taste.page.write rest-content: len([p for p in taste.panels(files) if not p.atRest]) == 0 -- block r6/luna-rare-ui: a demo shows its content before any input ("open" in an empty box fails)
C taste.page.write blank-region: len(taste.render(files).blankRegions) == 0 -- block r6/claude-landing: no 400 px band that is 97% one colour in the viewport-step captures after the reader walk (Claude's landing reveals were blank to a capture without the walk)
C taste.page.write first-screen: taste.render(files, viewports:"desktop").heroVisual >= 0.15 or taste.critique(files).axis("illustration").score >= 3 -- warn: the first screen carries a visual of the subject, or type that is itself the image

-- illustration and motion that serve the idea
C taste.page.write illustration-serves: taste.critique(files).axis("illustration").score >= 2 -- block: drawings depict the subject (a forest floor with mycelium), not a generic sphere, blob, orbit or gradient
C taste.page.write motion-named: taste.render(files).autoMotion <= 1 or taste.concept().motion != null -- warn frontend-design(idea): one orchestrated motion on load at most, and the concept record says what it shows
C taste.page.write reduced-motion: taste.render(files).reducedMotionRunning == 0 -- block design-craft#js-motion-reduced: with prefers-reduced-motion nothing loops and no rAF animation runs
C taste.page.write motion-answers: taste.critique(files).axis("motion").score >= 2 -- warn: motion answers an action or explains a change; no fade-up on every section

-- type, color and spacing craft
C taste.page.write families: len(taste.render(files).families) <= 3 -- warn frontend-design(idea): one or two families, plus mono only for code or data
C taste.page.write measure: 45 <= taste.render(files, viewports:"desktop").bodyMeasure <= 85 -- warn bringhurst: body lines of 45 to 85 characters
C taste.page.write body-size: taste.render(files).bodySize >= 16 and 1.35 <= taste.render(files).bodyLeading <= 1.8 -- warn: body text 16 px or more, leading 1.35 to 1.8
C taste.page.write hues: taste.render(files).hues <= 4 -- warn: at most 4 non-neutral hues outside drawings; one accent with a job
C taste.page.write contrast: taste.render(files).contrastFails == 0 -- block wcag#1.4.3: 4.5:1 body, 3:1 large, in light and dark
C taste.page.write tracked-caps: taste.render(files).trackedCaps <= 8 -- warn frontend-design(idea)+design-craft#uppercase: few tracked uppercase labels; round 3 measured 14 (Luna rare-ui) and 21 (Claude rare-ui) in the Edge prototype (Obscura's computed style reports 0), so this is a warn: Paul preferred the page with 21
C taste.page.write default-cluster: taste.critique(files).axis("color").evidence_count("default cluster") == 0 or taste.concept().rejected != [] -- warn frontend-design(idea): cream + serif + terracotta, black + acid green, broadsheet hairlines, the card kit, eyebrow chrome are defaults; use one only when the concept asks for it
C taste.page.write rhythm: taste.render(files).sectionPads <= 3 and taste.render(files, viewports:"desktop").leftEdges <= 8 -- warn: section spacing from at most 3 values; text starts on at most 8 left edges

-- nothing broken (the harness runs these on every round; failures are rows in the next diff with cause broken)
C taste.page.write dead-control: taste.render(files).dead == 0 -- block plan20#C13.2: every control changes something by pointer, keyboard and touch
C taste.page.write errors: taste.render(files).errors == 0 -- block plan20#C13.2: no console or page error in any variant
C taste.page.write overflow: taste.render(files, viewports:"phone").overflow <= 1 -- block: nothing wider than 390 px
C taste.page.write focus: len(taste.drive(files).focusInvisible) == 0 -- block wcag#2.4.7: every control shows focus

-- deterministic page checks (src/grant_agent/taste_checks.py): the host runs them on every review with no model call, seals the
-- result into the round (page-checks.json), sends failures to the critic as required difference rows and refuses done() on a block.
-- Each one is a defect the image critic passed on the r9 Luna landing (87.5/100), measured on its real round 1, 2 and 4 renders.
A taste.page.check(files:[path] render:render) -> [{check:str level:block|warn passed:bool hits:[str]}] -- reads the deliverable and the render's captures; prompt view: check, found, fix
I taste.page.check reads:files,render impl:src/grant_agent/taste_checks.py
C taste.page.check theme-dark: taste.page.check(files).passed("theme-dark") -- block r9/luna-landing#round-4: each dark capture is dark (median luma <= 110) and differs from its light capture; a page that declares prefers-color-scheme: dark but renders light is an invalid render (renderer gap: route to the browser owner, its dark tiles prove nothing); a page with no dark theme is a page defect
C taste.page.check side-void: taste.page.check(files).passed("side-void") -- block r9+r6/luna-landing: no heading block with an empty left column (>= 25% of the content width, ink in <= 15% of its rows); an eyebrow alone in a wide column beside its heading was the lead's "large empty columns" in round 3 and is back in r9
C taste.page.check visible-dash: taste.page.check(files).passed("visible-dash") -- block no-slop#decorative-dash: no em dash, en dash or spaced hyphen as punctuation in visible text; "01 — CAPABILITIES" eyebrows on all three r9 sections
C taste.page.check stock-phrase: taste.page.check(files).passed("stock-phrase") -- block paul/r6+no-slop: nothing from the stock phrase seed list in visible text; r9 "Good help has a shape."
C taste.page.check abstract-art: taste.page.check(files).passed("abstract-art") -- warn r9/luna-landing: an inline illustration whose every drawn label is a process word (question, way through, decide, draft, checked) draws a metaphor; the critic then scores illustration <= 2 unless the drawing shows the subject itself
X taste.page.check side-void -> move the eyebrow above the heading and let the heading take the measure, or give the column real content (a fact table, a figure); never pad it with a decoration
X taste.page.check theme-dark -> render-ignored-dark-theme: do not repair the page, report the renderer gap; page-has-no-dark-theme: add dark tokens under prefers-color-scheme: dark
X taste.page.check visible-dash -> "01 — Capabilities" becomes "Capabilities", or drop the eyebrow: a 01/02 marker only for a real sequence

-- worked cases: three decisions shown on real renders. The host projects the cases that match the brief into the generator,
-- repair and critic prompts (taste_context.compact_manual), so a small model sees the decision, not just the rubric.
-- Crop regions are [x y w h] in pixels of the named capture; open them, they are the evidence. Each case distils the better page's
-- principle; its subject, facts, wording and layout stay out (C taste.page.write no-imitation).
T case{id:str applies:[str] principle:str checks:[str]}
T crop{side:before|after path:path region:[int] shows:str}
S taste.case h7 #3 [id applies principle checks]
E "demonstrate" [landing about presentation] "Every claim about what the subject does arrives with one instance a visitor can check on the page; facts fill the space beside a heading, or the heading takes it." [stock-phrase side-void abstract-art swap-test]
  E crop before "proof/r9/arm-luna/T1/evidence/landing/round-4/render/desktop-light.png" [140 1213 1160 435] "capabilities as three verb phrases (Find the signal, Make it legible, Build a first version) with icons; the eyebrow 01 — CAPABILITIES alone in a 430 px column beside the heading"
  E crop before "proof/r9/arm-luna/T1/evidence/landing/round-4/render/desktop-light.png" [140 74 1160 1043] "hero art: a tangled line resolving into sliders, labelled OPEN QUESTIONS, A WAY THROUGH, DECIDE: a metaphor of help, not help"
  E crop before "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-l-landing-d-light.jpg" [0 80 1440 1360] "round 3 Luna: Think with care. Make things real. A sphere with an orbit. 01 / WHAT I DO alone beside its heading"
  E crop after "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-c-landing-d-light.jpg" [150 1755 1140 1035] "five capabilities, each a small working instance: a note rewritten in four registers, a function with its one-line fix and the error it prevents, a reasoning trace, a chart of numbers"
  E crop after "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-c-landing-d-light.jpg" [150 1080 1140 540] "the eyebrow sits above the heading; the side column holds a fact table (made by, good at, works in) instead of air"
  E observe "The lead's look at r9 round 4 (5 Oct): the page says what it does only as claims (three verb phrases, a quote about drafts). On the better page every claim has a checkable instance under it, and the first screen names a concrete job."
  E reject "polishing the claims (bigger serif, better icons, another section): the r9 critic scored the first draft 87.5 with content and illustration at 4, five rounds of repairs polished it, and the page stayed generic"
  E reject "copying the better page's five tiles, its headline or its subjects (race condition, bat and ball): imitation, refused by no-imitation"
  E repair "keep the layout; under each capability replace the description with one before -> after instance from your own subject (an input line, the output line, labelled sample when it is sample); move the eyebrow above the heading; replace the metaphor art with the first instance drawn large"
  E not "a brief for a mood or brand piece with nothing to demonstrate; a subject that cannot be shown without inventing data (show a real artifact or say it is a sample); a count: three honest instances beat eight, and an atlas of interactions is case proportion"
E "mechanism" [rare uncommon interaction] "Rare lives in the defining mechanism working on the page, not in the name, the shape or the citation." [rare-only mechanism rest-content primary-sources]
  E crop before "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-l-rare-ui-d-light.jpg" [200 640 1040 300] "Radial action wheel: a pie menu that opens on tap, shown as one open disc in an empty panel, sourced to a GitHub widget and a CSS demo"
  E crop after "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-c-rare-ui-d-light.jpg" [150 4740 1140 560] "a marking menu in the same radial family: press and wait shows the menu, a quick flick selects without it, a counter shows menu uses against marks, credited Kurtenbach and Buxton, CHI 1994, in the plate"
  E crop after "proof/c13-taste/shots-edge-before-switch/r3-c-rare-ui-d-light.jpg" [150 2050 1140 530] "a bubble cursor at rest: the target cloud is drawn, the nearest target is always captured, and a toggle to an ordinary pointer lets the visitor feel the difference"
  E observe "Both pages show a radial menu; only one shows what makes it uncommon (selection by mark without display). The common one opens and waits, which every pie menu does; its panel is empty until clicked."
  E reject "keeping the wheel and citing the 1988 pie-menu paper: a primary source for a common widget is still a common widget"
  E reject "adding more specimens of the same kind to reach a count: six renamed widgets failed round 3; count never substitutes for mechanism"
  E repair "keep the radial layout; add the defining path: pointer down plus a stroke longer than 40 px selects the item in that direction without showing the menu, press and wait shows it; draw the six items faded around the centre and the last mark's ink trail at rest; credit author, venue and year in the plate"
  E not "a brief that does not ask for rare: a settings page should use the common widget people know; a mechanism that needs hardware the page cannot run (pressure, multi-touch); a mechanism you cannot make observable to the driver: then pick another candidate. Even the better page's marking pad is thin at rest; density still applies"
E "proportion" [any] "The brief's own ask sets the size: build what it names, at the depth it implies, and stop; a number from another brief or a rule never sets it." [proportion swap-test]
  E crop before "proof/r8/arm-luna/T1/evidence/landing/round-1/render/desktop-light.png" [160 2085 1120 1880] "a landing page that asked who you are, what you do, why use you, spends 40% of its height on Eight ways to keep the work steerable: marking menus, crossing, bubble cursor, drag-and-pop; the T2 rare-UI instruction had leaked into its prompt"
  E crop after "proof/r8/arm-luna/final/T1/evidence/landing/round-4/render/desktop-light.png" [645 1135 655 250] "after the prompt was scoped: one labelled sample request and its answer shows the capability in one place"
  E observe "A visitor learns less from eight mechanisms than from one example of the job. The brief asked three questions; the atlas answers none of them."
  E reject "relabelling the eight studies as capabilities or polishing them: the size, not the finish, is wrong"
  E reject "meeting a quantity from elsewhere (eight vernacular terms, a lot = 8, sixteen candidates): those were proxies and they leaked"
  E repair "delete the atlas section; keep the one study that shows a real capability and turn it into a labelled worked example; the page keeps three or four sections, one per question in the brief"
  E not "a brief that asks for many (a lot of rare elements, a gallery, a comparison of ten tools); a simple ask that still has 3+ comparable facts (a small table is proportionate, Paul expected structure on a simple r5 task); proportion is to the ask, not to minimal length"
J proportion fits|over|under: "Does the size of the page match what the brief asks, section by section?" -- over when a section answers no question in the brief or a count comes from elsewhere; under when an asked question has no section; fits otherwise

-- the loop: draft once, then difference and repair (C13.7)
C taste.diff.write rows: taste.diff.rows() >= 3 -- block plan20#C13.7: a difference report names at least 3 gaps; "no gaps" is only accepted when the anchor verdict is win
C taste.diff.write evidence: len([r for r in taste.diff.rows() if len(r.evidence) < 2]) == 0 -- block: every row cites one ref on each side
C taste.diff.write keeps: len([r for r in taste.diff.rows() if r.gap == 0]) >= 1 -- warn: name what already works so the repair leaves it alone
C taste.page.write targeted: taste.churn(files).ratio <= 0.5 or taste.diff.has_page_row() -- block plan20#C13.7: a repair round changes at most half the lines unless a row with scope page (concept or research) asks for it
C taste.page.write mapped: taste.churn(files).unmapped == 0 -- warn: every changed hunk answers a diff row
C taste.page.write no-imitation: taste.overlap(files, against).numbers <= 0.2 and taste.overlap(files, against).elements <= 0.5 -- block c13-manual-only#round-1: a repair against a same-brief result transfers the principle, not the content; in the proof all 8 elements of Luna's repair came from the better page's 13, with its exact fairy-ring numbers (20 cm, 150 years, 2,827 m2, 1,131 mushrooms)
C taste.page.write no-regress: taste.critique(files).mean >= previous.critique.mean -- block paul/r11: revert a repair whose taste score drops; newly introduced blocking checks enter the next repair and still prevent completion
C taste.page.write min-rounds: taste.rounds() >= 2 -- block plan20#C13.5: at least two critique-and-fix rounds for design work; no stopping at the first render
C taste.lesson quarantined: taste.lesson().state == "quarantine" -- block plan20#C9.3: lessons enter as frontier patches; only the Evolver promotes
C taste.lesson labels: taste.labels().qualityDecisive >= 30 and taste.labels().qualityRuns >= 3 and taste.judge().agreement > taste.judge().majorityBaseline or taste.lesson().state == "quarantine" -- block astra2#2+plan20#C9.3: automatic promotion stays quarantined until 30 decisive genuine quality labels from 3 blind rounds and a frozen quality judge above its majority baseline (src/grant_agent/taste_labels.py); "which one is Claude?" answers are identity guesses and never count as quality labels

-- L2 judgement points
J against anchor|other-arm|paul|previous: "Which better result is this round measured against?" -- paul when he gave words on this output (his words win); other-arm when a stronger output for the same brief exists; anchor from proof/taste-anchors by brief kind; previous only when nothing better exists, and then the critique's lowest axis is the target
J cause research|concept|content|density|visual|motion|type|color|spacing|finish|broken: "Where does this gap come from?" -- trace to the earliest stage: a page of common widgets is research, not visual; unrelated sections are concept; slogans are content
J scope element|section|page: "How much must change to close this gap?" -- element by default; section when the section's idea is wrong; page once per task, only for cause concept or research
J lesson promote|local|drop: "Would this gap repeat on the next brief of this kind?" -- promote when the cause is a habit (empty demo panels, slogans, pattern-library sources); local when it is about this subject; drop when it is taste noise the rubric does not score
J subject pick|given: "Does the brief give the subject?" -- pick: choose one subject with its own materials and words (fungi, herbaria, Solari boards) before any layout; given: list its vernacular first
J rare rare|common: "Would a front-end developer have built this element in the last year?" -- yes = common; rare needs a paper, archive or inventor's repo, and its defining mechanism working
J bold one|split: "Which one element should a visitor remember?" -- name it in the concept record; everything else gets quieter
J accessory keep|remove: "Finishing pass: which one decoration carries nothing?" -- remove it (an eyebrow, a rule, a badge, a second accent), then render again
J stop ship|repair|report: "After this round: is every block green, critique passed, anchor tie or win?" -- ship; else repair while rounds < 5; at 5 report what is still behind, with the last diff

-- procedures (host steps)
P research(brief:str): taste.brief(brief); J proportion; J subject; web.search and read the primary sources (papers, archives, inventors' repos) for 2x the count; J rare per candidate; taste.common(names); taste.research.write(rows) C candidates C rare-only
C taste.research goal: len(taste.research.used()) >= taste.brief(brief).count and taste.research.primary_share() >= 0.5 and len(taste.research.candidates()) >= 2 * len(taste.research.used()) -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes
P concept(brief:str): J subject; J bold; write one idea, the vernacular, the quiet parts, the motion (or none), and the defaults rejected with the cluster each one belongs to; taste.concept.write(concept) C ready
C taste.concept goal: taste.concept.ready() and taste.concept.before_layout() -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes
P draft(brief:str files:[path]): run taste.research(brief); run taste.concept(brief); taste.page.write(files) C concept-first C stock C dead-control C errors; taste.render(files); taste.critique(files)
C taste.draft goal: len(taste.render(files)) == 4 and len(taste.critique(files)) == 11 -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes
P repair(files:[path] against:path|str): J against; taste.critique(files, against); taste.diff.write(files, against) C rows C evidence C keeps; J cause per row; J scope per row; J lesson per row; taste.lesson(row, rule, check) C quarantined; taste.page.write(files) C targeted C mapped; taste.render(files); taste.critique(files) C no-regress
C taste.repair goal: taste.diff.rows_open() == 0 and taste.critique(files).mean >= previous.mean and taste.churn(files).ratio <= 0.5 -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes
P finish(files:[path]): J accessory; taste.page.write(files); taste.render(files); taste.drive(files) C dead-control C focus C errors C overflow; taste.gate(files); taste.anchor(files); J stop
C taste.finish goal: taste.gate(files).blocks == 0 and taste.render(files).dead == 0 and taste.render(files).errors == 0 and taste.critique(files).passed -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes
P make(brief:str files:[path]): run taste.draft(brief, files); run taste.repair(files, against); run taste.repair(files, against) while not taste.critique(files).passed and taste.rounds() < 5; run taste.finish(files)
C taste.make goal: taste.gate(files).blocks == 0 and taste.critique(files).passed and taste.anchor(files).verdict in ["tie", "win"] and taste.rounds() >= 2 -- block plan20#C13+cl1.1#5: the procedure goal; run returns -G and done() is refused until it passes

-- fixes
X taste.research.write rare-only -> drop the common element; take the next candidate from the research table whose source is a paper or archive (HCI museum, ACM DL, Buxton collection, the inventor's site)
X taste.page.write empty-panel -> fill the panel at rest with the thing itself: draw the menu's items faded, render the table, show the first specimen; or shrink the panel to its content
X taste.page.write blank-region -> render the canvas on load, not on intersection only; reveals start visible and animate from 96% opacity, never from 0 behind a scroll trigger
X taste.page.write stock -> replace the slogan with the most specific true sentence about the subject (a number, a name, a date); if none exists, delete the line
X taste.page.write concept-coverage -> rewrite each section's example content in the subject's words (the tree view becomes a taxonomy of the subject, the table holds the subject's data)
X taste.page.write targeted -> revert, then apply only the diff rows; one hunk per row
X taste.page.write reduced-motion -> wrap every loop and rAF in a matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)") guard and draw the final frame
X taste.page.write no-imitation -> keep the gap's principle (one subject, primary sources, content at rest) and pick your own subject, elements and numbers from your research table
X taste.diff.write rows -> compare axis by axis with the rubric; the lowest-scoring axes always yield a row
X taste.page.write default-cluster -> say in the concept which cluster you chose and why, or move one axis (palette, type, layout) to the subject's own materials

-- frontier
F commonness seed list for config/c13/commonness.json (Codex owns the file): card, modal, dialog, carousel, accordion, tabs, toast, tooltip, drawer, sidebar, navbar, breadcrumb, stepper, progress bar, skeleton loader, toggle switch, segmented control, chips, slider, range slider, timeline scrubber, split view, resizable panes, tree view, command palette, kbar, cmdk, radial menu, pie menu, hold to confirm, long press button, kanban, infinite scroll, masonry grid, glassmorphism, neumorphism, gradient blob, parallax hero, marquee, typewriter text, scroll progress, dark mode toggle, theme switcher, search with autocomplete, date picker, color picker, file dropzone, rating stars, pricing table, testimonial carousel, FAQ accordion, bento grid, sticky header
F stock phrase seed list (taste.text.stock): think with care, make things real, what comes next, made for what comes next, curated for the curious, collected in the wild, in motion, at the center, open possibility, from what if, let's make a start, your next good question, bring me the task, good help, more capable, built for, designed for, crafted, reimagined, the future of, a new way to, everything you need
F panel ink needs a pixel measure as well as boxes (a drawn canvas has no text box); c13_render.mjs today flags empty only at < 8 words and no media, which passes Luna's round-3 panels -> Codex: add ink and gap from the screenshot crop
F Obscura 0.2.3 ignores prefers-color-scheme and prefers-reduced-motion emulation, loads no web fonts, lacks setPointerCapture and Playwright mouse moves; dark captures, type critique of web fonts, reduced-motion and drag checks stay undecided until the engine has them -> proof/c13-browser-gaps.md
F the preference adapter (src/grant_agent/browser_render_profile.js) answers matchMedia, so pages that set data-theme from script render dark (r7, r8: dark median luma 24-33), but CSS-only @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) rules stay unapplied: r9 Luna and the Claude anchor have dark captures identical to light (median 240); every critique of those dark tiles scored a light page -> browser owner: apply the rewritten media rules (or inject the dark block unwrapped) and prove it on proof/r9/arm-luna/T1/evidence/landing/round-4/artifact.html; C taste.page.check theme-dark blocks until then
F the critic sees the page; it does not feel drag latency or touch -> taste.drive reports per-control timing; motion score stays a judgement
F rare is relative to the agent's training data, not to the world; a commonness list goes stale -> lessons with cause research add entries through the C9 gate
F the frozen judge in taste_judge.py scores text features; image pairs need the critic's side-by-side until a calibrated image judge exists -> plan 20 C13.4

