M taste "Luna's rare-UI page used command palette, split view, slider, hold button, tree and radial menu in mostly empty panels; Claude's used magic lens, bubble cursor, marking menu, alphaslider, crossing and pull cord with illustrated plates and primary sources" src:plans/20-revolutionise-computer-and-browser-use.md#round-3-result author:lead state:verified
M taste "very easy to tell which was which; taste is not there and Luna's stuff is broken; the lead should have looked before sending" src:plans/20-revolutionise-computer-and-browser-use.md#round-3-result author:Paul state:verified
M taste "taste is not a plugin: question the output, report the difference against a better result, turn it into lessons, repair; first drafts are slow, repairs are fast" src:plans/20-revolutionise-computer-and-browser-use.md#C13.7 author:Paul state:verified
M taste "finish and taste (more niche, more polished); names things well; a small summary table; a real report" src:proof/preference-pairs.json#identityReasons.r5 author:Paul state:verified
M taste "filler language, decorative dashes and noise words are the tells" src:proof/preference-pairs.json#identityReasons.r4 author:Paul state:verified
M taste "rounds 1 to 3 asked only which side was Claude: those are identity guesses (recognizability), not quality labels; the v1 judge trained on them as preferences scored 5/18 against a 12/18 majority baseline" src:proof/preference-pairs.json+config/c13-identity-judge.json author:lead state:verified
M taste "the r8 T1 drafts received the T2 instruction to implement eight uncommon mechanisms, and both landings grew an eight-interaction atlas; the r9 prompt scopes it out, and taste.brief count no longer carries between briefs" src:proof/r8/arm-luna/T1/draft/prompt.txt author:lead state:verified
M taste "subject vernacular drives a distinct look; plan, then review the plan against the default before code; named clusters of generated pages; one bold element; one orchestrated motion; numbering only for sequences; screenshot self-critique; remove one accessory" src:github.com/anthropics/claude-code@dbdd79c/plugins/frontend-design/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md license:"All rights reserved (Anthropic commercial terms); ideas only, no text" author:"Prithvi Rajasekaran, Alexander Bricken" state:verified
M taste "body measure 45 to 75 characters, 66 ideal; a modular type scale" src:"Robert Bringhurst, The Elements of Typographic Style, 1992" author:Bringhurst state:verified
M taste "a capture without a reader walk showed Claude's landing sections blank (scroll reveals), and a full-page resize blanked its speed-zoom canvas; both render in a real viewport" src:proof/c13-taste/shots author:Claude state:verified
V P taste.make -> harness:codex why:"writes files; render, drive and gate are script"
V C taste.page.write -> script why:"render, panels, text, sources and churn are measured"
V A taste.critique -> model:large-vision why:"needs to look at the screenshots; one call per round"
V J cause -> model:small why:"the rubric axis and evidence already point at the stage"
V A taste.anchor -> script+model:large-vision why:"frozen text judge plus the critic's side-by-side"

-- motion, theming and voice: Paul's r10 preference, 5 Oct 2026. Anchor inspected locally; never project its source.
E "Motion that explains the work" [any]
  E observed "Claude landing proof/r6-blind/arm-c/landing.html: heading rise 1000ms cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1), second line +120ms; lede +450ms, actions +600ms. Scroll reveal 900ms with the same easing; button hover 200ms, arrow 250ms; tone-demo opacity 250ms, text swaps after 220ms. Theme button sets data-theme."
  E decision "Use one short entrance and animate an actual change in the demonstration. Hover and press show the control responding. Scroll reveals happen once, with content already readable if observation fails. Keep the rough-note into team-update demonstration, with its uncertainty intact."
  E repair "Provide an accessible light/dark toggle, initialized from the system preference; interpolate background, text and border tokens over 250ms ease-out. The anchor toggle exists, but smooth theme interpolation is a new requirement, not proven anchor behavior. Use 180ms ease-out hover, 100ms press, 350ms demonstration change. Animate at least two meaningful changes, not arbitrary moving decorations."
  E check "Normal entrance motion-0 and motion-650 must differ; interaction before/intermediate/settled captures must show the relevant change. Critic judges the ordered sequences, never awards motion from a still or declared CSS. Under reduced motion render the final state immediately: no loops, reveals, transitions or animation-frame mutation. The anchor's perpetual canvas rAF and code timers are defects to avoid."
E "Plain voice, specific work" [any]
  E before "r10 Luna landing: I turn a rough question into a clear next step. Useful when the next step is still fuzzy. Specific beats impressive sounding."
  E after "Proposed repair: I am an AI assistant. I can edit a note, explain code, or compare options. Here is a note rewritten for a team. The release date is still unknown."
  E decision "Show the work instead of claiming its value. No pitch phrases, promises, unsupported outcomes or invented details. Short sentences. Name the subject and action. Fit the voice to the subject: a paper catalogue states the mechanism and evidence; an assistant shows the input, output and limits."
  E keep "Keep the rough-note into team-update demo. Preserve release slipped, tests flaky, Mina checking and the uncertain date. Do not invent Thursday at 14:00 from a note that only says thurs?. Mark sample facts as samples. The proposed after copy is teaching, not a claim that the sealed r10 page already says it."
C taste.page.check motion-sequence: taste.render(files).motion.meaningful >= 2 -- block paul/r10: entrance frames and at least one relevant interaction sequence must change; at least two observed meaningful transitions; no CSS declaration substitutes for frames
C taste.page.check theme-toggle: taste.render(files).motion.themeToggle == true -- block paul/r10: actual light to dark to light interaction changes the page palette and returns it; normal theme change is smooth, reduced-motion change is immediate
C taste.page.check reduced-motion: taste.render(files).motion.reduced.changed == false -- block paul/r10: reduced-motion frames stay still and no active animation or transition runs; missing evidence blocks
C taste.page.check diagram-geometry: len(taste.render(files).diagramIssues) == 0 -- block paul/r10: SVG labels fit their node and viewport, labelled nodes do not overlap, connector endpoints meet node edges; uncertain geometry is reported, never passed

-- critique rubric (the harness sends this section to the critic with the screenshots; scores 0..4, each with a tile ref and region)
-- inputs: the brief, taste-concept.cl, tiles of desktop light (first screen + full page), phone light, desktop dark, the drive report, the anchor's tiles
-- output: one S taste.critique record, 11 rows: the 10 axes below plus "anchor"
J crit-fidelity s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Does the page do what the brief's key words demand, each one?" -- 0 misses the brief (common widgets for "rare"); 2 meets it partly (some rare, some common); 4 every element meets it and shows its defining mechanism. Calibration: r6 Luna rare-ui = 1, r6 Claude rare-ui = 4
J crit-concept s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "From the first screen alone, what is the one idea? Does every section serve it?" -- 0 no idea, a list of parts; 2 an idea in the hero only; 4 one idea named in a sentence and carried by every section. Calibration: r6 Luna rare-ui = 1 (six specimens, no subject), r6 Claude rare-ui = 4 (a field guide to fungi in 13 plates)
J crit-content s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Count lines that would fit an unrelated page unchanged (swappable). Are there real names, numbers, dates?" -- 0 mostly slogans; 2 some concrete lines among stock ones; 4 every line specific to this subject. Calibration: r6 Luna landing = 1 ("Think with care. Make things real."), r9 Luna landing = 2 ("Good help has a shape.", capabilities as verb phrases with no instance), r6 Claude landing = 3 ("Find the race condition") Voice is equally important: plain, specific, honest, short sentences, tone fits subject; no pitches or promises. Cite visible copy and propose a specific replacement. A marketing voice caps content at 2.
J crit-density s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Is any panel or section mostly empty at rest? Does space carry something?" -- 0 several blank panels; 2 one or two thin panels; 4 every panel shows its thing at rest, whitespace is rhythm not absence. Calibration: r6 Luna rare-ui = 1, r6 Claude rare-ui = 3 (crossing plate thin)
J crit-illustration s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Do drawings and images depict the subject, made for this page?" -- 0 none or stock shapes (sphere, blob, orbit); 2 decorative but on-subject; 4 illustration explains the subject (a cross-section under a lens). Calibration: r6 Luna landing = 1 (sphere with orbit), r9 Luna landing = 2 (a tangled line becoming sliders, labelled only with process words: a metaphor, not the subject), r6 Claude rare-ui = 4
J crit-motion s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Do ordered entrance, interaction and theme frame sequences show meaningful motion, with reduced-motion sequences still?" -- 0 loops and fade-ups everywhere or nothing moves where the idea needs it; 2 neutral; 4 motion carries the idea (split-flap letters arrive in order). Score 2 when the page has no motion and needs none
J crit-type s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Is the type chosen for this subject, set with a clear scale, measure and leading? Is the display type doing work?" -- 0 default stack, flat scale; 2 competent but generic; 4 type is part of the image and every level reads at a glance
J crit-color s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Is the palette from the subject's materials, one accent with a job, good in dark too? Which default cluster, if any?" -- 0 clashing or default with no reason; 2 tasteful default cluster; 4 palette belongs to the subject and holds in both themes. Note the cluster in evidence ("default cluster: cream serif terracotta"). Score dark only from a valid dark render: when the host check theme-dark failed, the dark tiles are not evidence and color is at most 2
J crit-spacing s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Is there one rhythm: consistent section spacing, aligned edges, grouped by space before lines?" -- 0 ragged; 2 even but monotone; 4 rhythm with clear grouping and a few deliberate breaks. Calibration: r9 Luna landing = 2 at most (an eyebrow alone in a 430 px column beside each heading)
J crit-finish s0|s1|s2|s3|s4: "Phone, dark, focus, empty and error states, details: does anything look unfinished or broken?" -- 0 broken controls or layout; 2 works with rough edges; 4 nothing to fix at phone, dark and keyboard. Any dead control or console error caps this at 1
J crit-anchor lose|tie|win: "Side by side with the anchor's screenshots, would Paul pick this one?" -- the reason names the axis that decides it
C taste.critique passed: min(scores) >= 2 and crit("fidelity") >= 3 and crit("concept") >= 3 and mean(scores) >= 3.0 and crit("anchor") in ["tie", "win"] and taste.render(files).dead == 0 -- block plan20#C13.1: the critique passes only with every axis at s2 or more, fidelity and concept at s3, mean 3.0, anchor tie or win, nothing dead
-- calibration set: proof/c13-taste/calibration.cl scores the four round-3 pages with this rubric; the critic is re-run on them and must land within 1 point per axis before the harness trusts it
